# DaedalusTGM-Exp (Models/DaedalusTGM-Exp): code, configs, tests, docs and small fixtures are
# tracked. Architecture and plan: docs/Architecture.md, docs/Terrain-SLM-Plan.md.
#
# Datasets, checkpoints and run output usually live on a separate data disk and are
# symlinked in. Root-level entries deliberately have NO trailing slash: git treats a
# symlink as a file, so `/data/` would miss a `data -> <data disk>/...` link.
# They are also root-anchored so they never match the code packages of the same name
# (terrain_slm/data/, terrain_slm/export/).

# --- Python environment (uv) -------------------------------------------------
# uv.lock stays tracked: it is what makes the env reproducible.
/venv
/.venv
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Data (GLO-30 DEM, WorldClim, derived shards) ----------------------------
/data
/shards
*.tif
*.tiff
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.zarr/
*.npy
*.npz

# --- Training output ---------------------------------------------------------
/dist
/checkpoints/*
/runs
/wandb
/logs
/reports
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors

# --- Export for Cenda (weights binaries + golden tensors) --------------------
/artifacts
*.onnx
*.engine

# --- Profiling ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.ncu-rep
*.nsys-rep
*.qdrep
*.sqlite
*.prof

# --- Small hand-made fixtures used by unit tests stay tracked ----------------
!tests/fixtures/**

# --- The shipped release is tracked (Git LFS) ----------------------------------
# The model folder the game loads (TGMPipe.DEFAULT_MODEL, checkpoints/exp2-r3: the DaedalusTGM-Exp-2 release built
# by scripts/make_release.py) is committed: its *.pt weights through Git LFS (root .gitattributes), release.json and
# ATTRIBUTION.md as normal files. Its native/ export (~144 MB, regenerated from the weights on first use) and anything
# else written into the folder stay ignored. Training runs (checkpoints/<run>/, checkpoints/exp2/*, exp2-r1, exp2-r2)
# stay ignored. Shipping a new model = a NEW directory name (the tile caches are keyed on it), these lines for it
# here, and its `git lfs track` line in the root .gitattributes.
# (EXP-1's v2 / v3 / v4 were tracked here in plain git until 2026-11-19: removed, WorldClim-trained.)
!/checkpoints/exp2-r3/
/checkpoints/exp2-r3/*
!/checkpoints/exp2-r3/*.pt
!/checkpoints/exp2-r3/release.json
!/checkpoints/exp2-r3/ATTRIBUTION.md
# written by the game's model setup (ModelSetup.java)
/.setup-unavailable
